      "content": "ABOUT THE MAJOR The History major gives students a broad familiarity with human history, both Western and world, as a means of developing critical understanding and insight into how they might live now and in the future. The program engages students in deliberately rigorous intellectual development, and particularly focuses on the influence of religion in history. The exploration and discovery of lived human experience in the past (of church and world) is informed by a Christian/Anabaptist worldview. Upon completion of the major, students will be prepared to pursue advanced study in the disciplines of history, theology and philosophy, and in fields such as secondary teaching, law, library science, archival management and public history. HISTORY COURSES Students in the History major will complete at least one upper-division course in five of the following areas: Ancient history Medieval, Renaissance or Reformation history Modern European history World history American history Religious or topical history **Agreement does not include all required courses for the major at FPU** This agreement lists courses that are prerequisites or may be completed prior to transfer to satisfy major requirements. All transfer courses must be completed with a grade of C- or better, and students must complete a minimum of 18 units in the major at FPU. Please contact an academic advisor to discuss the recommended sequence of courses, including courses that may count for both GE and major requirements. To view the full degree requirements, please refer to the Undergraduate Catalog: https://catalog.fresno.edu/index.php .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(22, 43, 132);\">ABOUT THE MAJOR</strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The History major gives students a broad familiarity with human history, both Western and world, as a means of developing critical understanding and insight into how they might live now and in the future. The program engages students in deliberately rigorous intellectual development, and particularly focuses on the influence of religion in history. The exploration and discovery of lived human experience in the past (of church and world) is informed by a Christian/Anabaptist worldview. Upon completion of the major, students will be prepared to pursue advanced study in the disciplines of history, theology and philosophy, and in fields such as secondary teaching, law, library science, archival management and public history. </span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(22, 43, 132);\">HISTORY COURSES</strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students in the History major will complete at least one upper-division course in five of the following areas:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Ancient history</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Medieval, Renaissance or Reformation history</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Modern European history</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">World history</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">American history</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Religious or topical history</span></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(169, 62, 58);\">﻿**Agreement does not include all required courses for the major at FPU**</strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This agreement lists courses that are prerequisites or may be completed prior to transfer to satisfy major requirements. All transfer courses must be completed with a grade of C- or better, and students must complete a minimum of 18 units in the major at FPU. Please contact an academic advisor to discuss the recommended sequence of courses, including courses that may count for both GE and major requirements.&nbsp;To view the full degree requirements, please refer to the Undergraduate Catalog: </span><a href=\"https://catalog.fresno.edu/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px;\">https://catalog.fresno.edu/index.php</a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.&nbsp;</span></p>"
